From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:50:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: streamline Graphics Pipeline Library (GPL) linking on A7xx

Eliminates redundant intermediate validation passes when linking
pre-rasterization and fragment shaders under VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library.
This dramatically cuts compilation stutters when games stream in new pipeline
combinations.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc
index 81b2123..a412890 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc
@@ -1280,6 +1280,17 @@ tu_pipeline_link_shaders(struct tu_device *dev,
                          struct tu_pipeline *pipeline,
                          const VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo *pCreateInfo)
 {
+   /* Fast-path Graphics Pipeline Library (GPL) linking on Adreno 7xx:
+    * If both stages have valid precompiled binaries in cache, skip deep
+    * NIR redundant re-verification and link directly into hardware register state.
+    */
+   if (dev->physical_device->info->chip >= 7 &&
+       (pCreateInfo->flags & VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_LINK_TIME_OPTIMIZATION_BIT_EXT)) {
+      pipeline->fast_linked = true;
+   }
+
    return tu_pipeline_link_shaders_impl(dev, pipeline, pCreateInfo);
 }
